  {
   "xml_index": 5,
   "xml_name": "L05_005_Fibonacci Recursive",
   "display_name": "Fibonacci Recursive",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <b>Fibonacci sequence</b> is a famous sequence of numbers where each term is the sum of the two terms before it, starting with <code>0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, ...</code> (the 0th term is 0, the 1st term is 1, the 2nd term is <code>0+1=1</code>, the 3rd term is <code>1+1=2</code>, and so on).</p>\n<p><b>Recursive breakup (the hint formula):</b></p>\n<pre>fib(n) = fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2)</pre>\n<p>This says: the <code>n</code>-th Fibonacci number is the sum of the two Fibonacci numbers before it. Notice this recursive case calls itself <b>twice</b>.</p>\n<p><b>Termination condition (base cases):</b> this problem needs <b>two</b> base cases, not just one - <code>fib(0)</code> is defined directly as <code>0</code>, and <code>fib(1)</code> is defined directly as <code>1</code>. Without both of these, the two-way recursion above wouldn't have a safe place to stop.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a recursive function named <code>fib</code> that takes one parameter <code>n</code>, a <b>non-negative integer (int &gt;= 0)</b>, and returns the <code>n</code>-th Fibonacci number (0-indexed), using the recursive breakup and base cases given above.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>fib(6)</code> should return <code>8</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Base case examples:</b> <code>fib(0)</code> should return <code>0</code>, and <code>fib(1)</code> should return <code>1</code>, both directly (no recursion needed).</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def fib(n):\n    # write your code here (remember: this problem needs TWO base cases)\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(fib(6))",
