  {
   "xml_index": 6,
   "xml_name": "L05_006_Sum Of Digits Recursive",
   "display_name": "Sum Of Digits Recursive",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's write a recursive function that adds up the digits of a number. For example, the digits of <code>1234</code> are <code>1, 2, 3, 4</code>, which sum to <code>10</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Recursive breakup (the hint formula):</b></p>\n<pre>sum_of_digits(n) = (n % 10) + sum_of_digits(n // 10)</pre>\n<p>This says: the digit sum of <code>n</code> is its <b>last</b> digit (<code>n % 10</code>) plus the digit sum of everything <i>except</i> the last digit (<code>n // 10</code>) - a number with one fewer digit, moving closer to the base case.</p>\n<p><b>Termination condition (base case):</b> we stop when <code>n &lt; 10</code>, i.e. <code>n</code> is already a single digit - its digit sum is just itself, with no more digits to peel off.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a recursive function named <code>sum_of_digits</code> that takes one parameter <code>n</code>, a <b>positive integer (int &gt; 0)</b>, and returns the sum of its digits, using the recursive breakup and base case given above.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>sum_of_digits(1234)</code> should return <code>10</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Base case example:</b> <code>sum_of_digits(7)</code> should return <code>7</code> directly (no recursion needed).</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def sum_of_digits(n):\n    # write your code here (remember: base case first, then the recursive case)\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(sum_of_digits(1234))",
