  {
   "xml_index": 8,
   "xml_name": "L05_008_Collatz Steps Recursive",
   "display_name": "Collatz Steps Recursive",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>The <b>Collatz conjecture</b> is a famous unsolved problem in mathematics. Starting from any positive integer <code>n</code>, repeat the following rule: if <code>n</code> is even, divide it by 2; if <code>n</code> is odd, multiply it by 3 and add 1. Keep repeating with the new value. It is conjectured (though not proven!) that no matter which positive integer you start with, you will always eventually reach <code>1</code>.</p>\n<p>For example, starting from <code>6</code>: <code>6 -&gt; 3 -&gt; 10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 16 -&gt; 8 -&gt; 4 -&gt; 2 -&gt; 1</code>. That took <b>8 steps</b> to reach 1.</p>\n<p><b>Recursive breakup (the hint formula):</b> we want to count the number of steps needed to reach 1.</p>\n<pre>if n is even:\n    collatz_steps(n) = 1 + collatz_steps(n // 2)\nif n is odd:\n    collatz_steps(n) = 1 + collatz_steps(3 * n + 1)</pre>\n<p>Each recursive call performs one \"step\" of the Collatz rule, and adds 1 to the step count.</p>\n<p><b>Termination condition (base case):</b> we stop when <code>n == 1</code> - we have already arrived, so it takes <code>0</code> further steps.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a recursive function named <code>collatz_steps</code> that takes one parameter <code>n</code>, a <b>positive integer (int &gt; 0)</b>, and returns the number of steps needed to reach 1 using the Collatz rule, using the recursive breakup and base case given above.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>collatz_steps(6)</code> should return <code>8</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Base case example:</b> <code>collatz_steps(1)</code> should return <code>0</code> directly (no recursion needed - we're already there).</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def collatz_steps(n):\n    # write your code here (remember: base case first, then the two recursive cases)\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(collatz_steps(6))",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(collatz_steps(6))",
