  {
   "xml_index": 13,
   "xml_name": "L05_013_Count Occurrences Recursive",
   "display_name": "Count Occurrences Recursive",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's extend the previous question: instead of just checking <b>whether</b> a value appears, let's count <b>how many times</b> it appears in the list, from a given starting position onward.</p>\n<p><b>Recursive breakup (the hint formula):</b></p>\n<pre>count_occurrences(lst, index, target):\n    if lst[index] == target: 1 + count_occurrences(lst, index + 1, target)\n    otherwise: count_occurrences(lst, index + 1, target)</pre>\n<p>This says: the count from position <code>index</code> onward is <code>1</code> more than the count from <code>index + 1</code> onward, <i>if</i> the element at <code>index</code> matches <code>target</code> - otherwise, it's exactly the same as the count from <code>index + 1</code> onward.</p>\n<p><b>Termination condition (base case):</b> we stop when <code>index == len(lst)</code> - we've walked off the end of the list, so there are <code>0</code> more matches to count.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Define a recursive function named <code>count_occurrences</code> that takes a list <code>lst</code>, a starting index <code>index</code>, and a value <code>target</code>, and returns how many times <code>target</code> appears from position <code>index</code> to the end of the list. Write the full function definition yourself, using the recursive breakup and base case given above.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>count_occurrences([4, 7, 4, 2, 4, 9, 7], 0, 4)</code> should return <code>3</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Base case example:</b> <code>count_occurrences([4, 7, 4, 2, 4, 9, 7], 0, 100)</code> should return <code>0</code> (100 doesn't appear at all).</p>",
   "answerpreload": "# Define a recursive function named count_occurrences that takes:\n#   lst (a list), index (an int - the starting position), target (the value to count)\n# It should return how many times target appears from position index to the end of lst.\n# Remember: base case first, then the recursive case.\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(count_occurrences([4, 7, 4, 2, 4, 9, 7], 0, 4))",
